    {
      "text": "Fading in and out after 2-3 months These headphones worked great for about two and a half months. Now one of the headphones constantly fades in and out while fully charged. They sometimes have trouble staying connected as a pair. When these headphones are working they\u2019re great. When they\u2019re not working they\u2019re incredibly frustrating.",
      "occurrences": 2,
      "distinct_products": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "TERRIBLE AVOID like the PLAGUE!! TERRIBLE Camera. I loved it for the first 4-5 months. It worked as designed and seemed great.<br />However as time passed it began to have MASSIVE ISSUES.<br />It just beeps randomly now until reset. It does not record more than 2-3 mins on each file then the video dies and you just get audio, which is useless in a wreck.<br />Then as time went on the menus glitched out displaying garbage.<br />Now the video is upside down and the menus are so hosed you can't correct it.<br />The screen just glitches out when shutting down. it no longer shuts down correctly, the screen just flickers until the battery dies.<br />Had to replace the unit with a new brand this was GARBAGE.<br />Look elsewhere if you need a camera for more than 6 months..",
      "occurrences": 2,
      "distinct_products": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "BUYER BEWARE - NOT DUAL LINK DVI All of these cheap Cables Unlimited branded dual-link DVI cables are NOT dual link. The pins look like the cable _should be dual link_ but the cable itself is wired for single-link only.<br /><br />The 5-star reviews for this product are all for low-resolution monitors that only require single link.<br /><br />BUYER BEWARE",
      "occurrences": 2,
      "distinct_products": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "BEWARE! THIS RUINED MY THUMB JOINT I used the a Logitech trackball mouse both at home & work. After about 1 1/2 years I had to have surgery to replace the trapeziometacarpal (TMC) joint (Trapezium bone). I can't say this will definitely happen to you but it is a distinct possibility. The surgeon said that she had seen this same injury from other trackball users. I loved using a trackball so much that I switched to the style with a center ball so I could use your index & middle finger.",
      "occurrences": 2,
      "distinct_products": 2
    },
    {
